Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Explicit viscoelastic equation derivation", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9465504497732477`*^9, 
  3.946550457243265*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"45f584d2-c5b3-475a-a2fc-\
3355ce3c1137"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook includes code to solve for explicit representations of common \
viscoelastic constitutive equations. These equations are tensor equations \
relating an applied stress sigma (denoted here as s) to a strain rate gamma \
dot (denoted here as g). These two tensors are symmetric tensors and so each \
have six independent components. Common use cases include calculating the \
stress resulting from an imposed strain and calculating strain from an \
imposed stress. We are concerned with shear-rheometer geometries, which \
somewhat simplifies the resulting math. In particular, we assume that \
derivatives in the x direction are all 0 by symmetry. 

When solving for stress from an input strain, we will solve the extra stress \
equations to find the extra stress \[Tau] then find the total stress \
\[Sigma]=\[Tau]+\[Eta]s \[Gamma]. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.946550474898273*^9, 3.946550488448346*^9}, {
  3.946550578744047*^9, 
  3.946550773937409*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"012d64c7-06fa-4210-8935-\
ad39e7c710bc"],

